    "durationMs": 169826,
    "finalText": "The URL shortener is complete and fully verified. What I built:\n\n- **`app/`** — FastAPI app with `POST /links` (auto-generated or custom codes, 409 on duplicates), `GET /links/{code}`, `GET /r/{code}` (302 + atomic `UPDATE ... clicks = clicks + 1 RETURNING` so clicks increment exactly once even under concurrency), and `GET /links` (ascending creation order with `total`). URLs are validated as plain strings with `urlsplit` (http/https + host required) so they're stored and returned unchanged — no normalization. Global exception handlers put an `error` field on every 404/409/422, including malformed JSON.\n- **Persistence** — SQLAlchemy 2.0 model + Alembic migration (with a unique constraint on `code`); DB settings come from `DATABASE_URL` via pydantic-settings, normalized to the installed psycopg3 driver (`postgresql+psycopg://`).\n- **`start.sh`** — executable, runs `alembic upgrade head` then serves uvicorn in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000` (dependencies were already installed, so nothing is installed at start time).\n- **`requirements.txt`** pins the preinstalled versions (no extra packages needed); README documents startup.\n\nI tested all 34 scenarios against the running server — creation, custom codes, duplicates, redirects, click counting, listing order, and every 404/409/422 case — then restarted the server and confirmed data and click counts survived. The test rows were truncated afterward, so the harness starts with an empty table."
